# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#   /          -> dist/index.html      (static, non-WASM landing page)
#   /app/<pg>  -> dist/app/index.html  (WASM SPA host; client-side router takes over)
# The 200 status rewrites without changing the URL, so a deep link or hard reload
# inside the app (e.g. /app/portfolio) loads the SPA host instead of the landing page.
#
# These are enumerated per-route on purpose. A glob (/app/*  ->  /app/index.html)
# is REJECTED by Cloudflare Pages' loop detector — the destination /app/index.html
# itself matches /app/*, so Pages flags it as an infinite loop and silently drops
# the rule, and every deep-link reload falls through to the landing page at /.
# Exact sources don't collide with /app/index.html, so they're accepted.
# When you add a top-level app route, add a line here.
/app             /app/index.html   200
/app/login       /app/index.html   200
/app/portfolio   /app/index.html   200
/app/pricer      /app/index.html   200
/app/scenarios   /app/index.html   200
/app/tax         /app/index.html   200
